# AI Job Hunting Assistant — Cursor lessons

## GitHub push vs commit date (2026-07)

- `git status` “up to date with origin/main” means local and remote share the same commit SHA — the push already succeeded.
- GitHub Commits page shows **author/committer date**, not push date. Uploading an older local commit tonight still lists that commit under its original date (e.g. Jul 12).
- If the user wants a **today-dated** GitHub entry, create a new commit (or annotated tag/release) and push — do not expect push alone to change commit dates.
- HTTPS push needs a PAT or `gh auth`; empty working tree = nothing new to commit even if file mtimes look newer.

## PDF resume export layout (2026-07)

- Google Docs uploaded PDFs use subset TimesNewRoman fonts. Re-using those embedded font buffers via `insert_textbox` / `TextWriter` injects NBSP (`\xa0`) and soft hyphens (`\xad`) into output text.
- Built-in PyMuPDF font name on this environment is `tiro` / `Times-Roman` (not `times`). `●` / `•` glyphs are missing from Base-14 fonts — draw a filled circle for bullets instead.
- Never partially redact multi-line bullets (leaves stray `s` / `,`). Always full-width redact every wrapped line of the bullet, then rewrite.
- Existing SUMMARY must be replaced as a full section (clear everything between SUMMARY header and WORK EXPERIENCE), not per-bullet patches — otherwise old and new bullets overlap.
- Summary mods (`summary_suggestion` / `summary_bullet`) should not go through `modifications_to_replacements`; use `apply_summary_section_replace` / `apply_summary_insertion` instead.
